{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Use the existing Spring XD (eXtreme Data) Gradle-based codebase as the starting point; no architectural redesign is required.",
    "Performance tests (U1) will leverage the existing spring-xd-benchmark / perf-test modules rather than introduce a new test framework.",
    "Kafka client library version 0.8.1 and 0.8.2 are installed side-by-side via classpath swap (no in-place upgrade), as the goal is head-to-head comparison.",
    "Reactor 2.0.3 (U2) is treated as a binary-compatible drop-in replacement within the same 2.0.x line; the upgrade is implemented purely as a dependency version bump in the root build.gradle with no source refactor unless compatibility issues are found.",
    "JMX (U3) will be disabled by flipping the default value of the existing `enableJmx` style configuration property; opt-in is preserved by allowing users to re-enable it.",
    "Gradle build fixes (U4) will be limited to the `./gradlew dist` and `distZip` tasks; no migration to a new Gradle version is in scope.",
    "Compiler/javadoc warning cleanup (U5) will prefer source-level fixes over blanket `@SuppressWarnings` and will target only warnings currently emitted by the default build.",
    "Multi-instance RPM support (U6) will reuse the existing spec file structure and introduce instance-specific init scripts, following the standard SysV/systemd patterns already used in the project; configuration will be parameterized via a single /etc/sysconfig/xd-container file.",
    "Documentation updates (U7, U8) will use the existing Asciidoctor documentation source set; navigation/anchors are added rather than restructuring the doc tree.",
    "All work is performed by a single experienced developer who is deeply familiar with the Spring XD codebase."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Test infrastructure (Kafka 0.8.1 and 0.8.2 clusters, HDFS sink target, three transport configurations) is already available and can be reused.",
    "The Reactor 2.0.3 API is source- and binary-compatible with the version currently in use (2.0.x), so the upgrade is limited to a dependency change.",
    "The Gradle dist/distZip failures are localized to task wiring/dependencies and do not require a Gradle version migration.",
    "Compiler and javadoc warnings are finite and primarily concentrated in a small number of modules; no new module is in scope.",
    "The existing RPM spec file already supports a single xd-container instance; only the launch/init layer needs to be parameterized.",
    "OOTB batch jobs and analytics tab widgets are stable and not undergoing functional changes in this increment, so the documentation effort is purely editorial.",
    "A standard 8-hour workday is used for effort estimates; no parallel work is assumed.",
    "No external code review, release engineering, or packaging/sign-off effort is included beyond basic integration testing."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Project setup, planning, and environment preparation",
      "activity_description": "Read the relevant module sources, set up the local build, verify Kafka 0.8.1/0.8.2 and HDFS test endpoints are reachable, and confirm the baseline build is green before making changes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Performance test harness setup",
      "activity_description": "Configure the three sink/transport combinations (In-Memory Transport > Hdfs, Direct Binding Transport > Hdfs, Kafka > Hdfs) and the three payload types (baseline, Tuple, Serialized) for both Kafka 0.8.1 and 0.8.2 in the existing perf-test module.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Execute performance tests",
      "activity_description": "Run the configured matrix of payload x transport x Kafka-version scenarios, capturing throughput, latency, and resource metrics for each run; iterate on warm-up/cooldown as needed for stable results.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Analyze results and document comparison",
      "activity_description": "Aggregate the captured metrics into a side-by-side 0.8.1 vs 0.8.2 comparison and publish the findings as a short performance report attached to the increment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Upgrade Reactor to 2.0.3",
      "activity_description": "Bump the Reactor version property in the root build.gradle, resolve any compile/test fallout, run the affected module test suites, and update any deprecated API call sites uncovered by the build.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Disable JMX by default",
      "activity_description": "Change the default value of the JMX enablement flag so JMX is off out of the box, ensure the opt-in path still works, and add/adjust a unit test to lock in the new default.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.75
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Fix Gradle dist and distZip targets",
      "activity_description": "Reproduce the failures in `./gradlew dist` and `distZip`, identify the misconfigured task wiring or missing distribution content, apply the fix, and confirm the publish artifact is produced correctly.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Clean up compiler warnings",
      "activity_description": "Capture the current compiler warning list, address each one (cast warnings, deprecations, raw types, unchecked, etc.) with source-level fixes where reasonable, and re-run the build to confirm zero new warnings.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Clean up javadoc warnings",
      "activity_description": "Resolve javadoc warnings (missing/incorrect tags, malformed references, HTML issues) across the modules touched by the increment and re-run the javadoc task to confirm a clean output.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Multi-instance RPM script support (implementation)",
      "activity_description": "Parameterize the existing RPM init script so that multiple xd-container instances can be started/stopped on the same node, add per-instance configuration files, and ensure ports/data dirs do not collide.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Multi-instance RPM script support (testing and docs)",
      "activity_description": "Install the rebuilt RPM in a clean VM, start two or more xd-container instances, verify start/stop/status, and update the RPM administration section of the docs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "U7 - OOTB batch job documentation anchors and cross-references",
      "activity_description": "Add named anchors/ids to each OOTB batch job section and a top-level index so users can jump directly to a given job; verify links resolve in both HTML and PDF outputs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.25
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Analytics tab widget documentation",
      "activity_description": "Document each analytics tab widget, its inputs, and how it is wired into a streaming pipeline, with example snippets drawn from the existing reference apps.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.25
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "Integration and regression testing",
      "activity_description": "Run the full unit and integration test suite, smoke-test the container start-up path, and verify the new RPM, build, and configuration changes do not regress existing behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "Final review, cleanup, and hand-off",
      "activity_description": "Tidy up any leftover debug code, verify the gradle build is warning-free, review the documentation diffs, and summarize the changes for the increment's release notes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 20.25
  }
}
```

